Description: Use a standalone pwd helper for spawn-through-symlink tests
Author: Peios maintainers
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-09-16

The three spawn/chdir variants invoke pwd through subdir/pwd-symlink while
passing argv[0]=pwd. Peiosutils intentionally dispatches by the kernel's
executed path when those names differ, so this helper exits before exercising
getcwd. Prefer the declared standalone GNU build helper, already first in the
native PATH, for the explicit symlink case too. Reference roots without that
private helper retain upstream's original selection. No libc code, spawn
operation, PATH-search case or expected result changes.

--- a/posix/tst-spawn-chdir.c
+++ b/posix/tst-spawn-chdir.c
@@ -61,7 +61,12 @@
 const char *
 get_pwd_program (void)
 {
-  const char *const paths[] = { "/bin/pwd", "/usr/bin/pwd" };
+  /* This test invokes pwd through a differently named symlink.  The native
+     Peios multicall userland deliberately dispatches by the kernel's executed
+     path, not argv[0].  Use the declared standalone build utility when present;
+     reference distributions retain their ordinary standalone pwd program.  */
+  const char *const paths[] = { "/usr/libexec/coreutils-build/pwd",
+                              "/bin/pwd", "/usr/bin/pwd" };
   for (size_t i = 0; i < array_length (paths); ++i)
     if (access (paths[i], X_OK) == 0)
       return paths[i];
